---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/data.ts';
---
<Base title="How we make money" description="CryptoScanner is funded by affiliate commissions on some provider links. Here is exactly how that works and what it does not change." canonicalPath="/how-we-make-money">
<div class="prose">
  <h1>How we make money</h1>
  <p>CryptoScanner is free to use, with no account, no lead form and no sales calls. Some providers run affiliate or referral programmes: if you open an account or order a card after clicking one of our links, the provider may pay us a commission. It costs you nothing extra and you may, in some programmes, receive the same welcome offer as any other new customer.</p>
  <h2>What this changes — and what it doesn't</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Monetised links are marked "affiliate link" and carry <code>rel="sponsored"</code>. Links without confirmed affiliate access go to the official site and say so.</li>
    <li>Commissions never affect which cards are listed, how they are ranked or the figures shown. A card without any affiliate programme can rank above one that pays us.</li>
    <li>We publish no sponsored placements today; if we ever do, they will be separate and labelled.</li>
    <li>We do not sell your data and we do not need your identity, wallet or bank details. Identity checks happen with the provider, never with us.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Where we stand</h2>
  <p>Affiliate programmes are listed on each card as a status: none, identified, terms verified, applied, accepted, tracking tested, payment observed. We only call a link "affiliate" once access is confirmed. We never fabricate referral codes.</p>
  <p>Questions or concerns: <a href={url('/contact')}>contact us</a>.</p>
</div>
</Base>
